From 31939c0e0391940109a6be18cad39eb4c9ca68a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 09:56:15 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] MPEG: accept toIPU DMA with decoder backpressure

Forward normal and source-chain channel 4 transfers to the FFmpeg decoder for games that own their bitstream ring. Invoke the registered Nodata callback through the scheduler and publish completion for native sceMpegIsEnd.

Query readiness before consuming a DMA tag on restart. Feeding while eight pictures were queued ran past Sofdec REFE boundaries, made the readable block count negative, and replayed stale video data. Leave channel addresses unchanged until the decoder has room.

Build: clean ps2_runtime with FFmpeg enabled, no game data or diagnostics.
